		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Bullet 2.37 released: btStackAlloc]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2618#p2618"><![CDATA[
Bullet 2.37 has just some minor changes:<br><br>- added unfinished btHeightfieldTerrainShape.cpp/h. Needs work to create the triangles (and potentially optimized CollisionAlgorithms for certain cases)<br>- removed default construction of btDiscreteDynamicsWorld/btCollisionWorld.<br>User needs to pass data explicitly. This is in order to reduce dependencies.<br>- Internal change: Added btStackAlloc, to allow fast allocations in a FIFO style. Was used in btGjkEpa, exposed it into btCollisionWorld.<br>- Internal change: renamed ConcaveShape to btConcaveShape<br><br><a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/mediawiki-1.5.8/index.php?title=Download" class="postlink">Download page for Bullet Physics SDK</a><br><br>Thanks,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Wed Nov 29, 2006 3:11 am</p><hr />
